WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.100
- In order to belong in this
tribe, you have to conform,

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:10.363
and if you have doubts,
you're a dangerous person.

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:13.610
How many leaders have been
built up in these mega churches

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:16.033
that fall because the
pressure's just too much.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.400
And as I look back, we were two kids

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.133
trying so hard to get it right.

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:23.263
My name is Lisa Gungor.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:26.873
I'm a recent author, I'm a
musician and a songwriter.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:32.760
My mom and I found this wild church.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.300
They called themselves the Holy Rollers,

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.770
and from the moment you
walked in, it was loud

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:39.003
and people were running around the church.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.600
I just think it's awesome.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.220
So while a lot of people think it's crazy,

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:46.683
filled with crazy people,
I loved it and I was in.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:51.740
I ended up going to college
and I start dating this boy

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.693
who's super Christian.

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:58.960
We get married really young.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.640
We're too young to even rent
a car when we're married.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:02.840
We didn't drink or cuss.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:07.500
So we end up getting a
job at a really big church

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:08.493
in Michigan.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:12.960
And this church was the
size of a mall, it's huge,

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.533
it was about 10,000 people.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:16.550
We built a house out in the country.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:19.360
They paid for our car, for our gas.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.630
They paid for Michael's school.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:25.120
We were 20 years old, and
we had this dream job.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.440
We didn't have sex with each
other before we were married.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.370
We waited to kiss, we did it all right,

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.680
we had this transactional ideal of God

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:35.943
and that's why we landed this
really great, awesome job.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.310
We started trying to get pregnant
and couldn't get pregnant

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:41.610
and people would tell me,
well, just pray and believe.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:43.893
Like, just say it and it will happen.

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:47.910
And I thought, I just don't
know how that can be true.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:50.090
We were traveling the world,
we were going overseas

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:54.223
and playing to sometimes
60,000 people in arenas.

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:57.103
The more we ran into
other people's stories,

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.220
the more we started doubting
what we'd been given.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.730
Michael and I took this trip in Europe.

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:04.920
From Rome, we took trains up to Krakow.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.283
We visited the concentration camps.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:11.143
We walked through the crematoriums.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:14.260
And it's real hard to come back to America

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:17.990
and pray for something
when you have these images

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:21.770
of people's hair in piles and
children's shoes in piles.

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:24.260
Your ideas on what a good God is

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:26.023
can change pretty dramatically.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.330
So I came back and found
myself trying to pray

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.750
for us to have a baby
or pray for our church

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.320
or pray for these different things,

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:36.930
and I just kept thinking
about the concentration camp

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:40.930
and how my whole perspective on my faith

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:42.663
has been a transaction.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:44.530
If I'm good enough or if I pray enough

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:48.000
or if I believe enough,
then I get blessings

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.053
and I get a baby or a good life.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:53.453
It's not how life is.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:56.210
We all have this perspective
on who is in and who is out.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:58.593
For Michael and I, that
began to change slowly.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:02.393
You have to conform
and if you have doubts,

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:04.373
you're a dangerous person.

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:08.713
I remember looking around
going, what am I doing here?

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:11.850
What am I building with my life?

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:14.960
We realized we're no good
for this place that we're at

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:17.600
because our ideas had changed so much

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.293
and that we needed to leave.

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:23.020
I started weeping and
crying and freaking out,

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:25.250
going, what are we doing, we
don't know what we're doing.

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:26.760
Do you realize what we just left?

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:28.393
We left all of our security.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:33.073
And we started becoming
heretics, you know.

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:36.030
We go up to Denver, we end up starting

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:38.500
a little house church in our apartment.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.190
Our whole goal for it
was that it was inclusive

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:44.390
and that it was vulnerable
and that it was this place

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.300
that we'd always dreamed of church being.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.360
More questions and more doubt

00:03:48.936 --> 00:03:51.060
were arising for Michael and I.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:54.170
Our heretic levels kept
shifting and changing

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:56.263
and kind of one-upping each other.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:01.100
Eventually, Michael and I, we get pregnant

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:03.960
and I was really glad for that
because it didn't feel like

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:05.803
our daughter was this answer.

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:09.010
We really went through this
trial and this suffering

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:11.133
and now we're getting this baby girl.

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.453
Our ideas of God are deconstructing.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.300
What is that we still believe?

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:18.382
But Michael looks at me and just says,

00:04:18.382 --> 00:04:20.693
I don't believe in God anymore,

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:22.120
like I can't believe any of it,

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:24.033
and he just ends up talking more.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:27.460
And I remember just
freezing in my whole body

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:30.770
'cause there's always been,
I was okay with the questions

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:32.793
but I wasn't okay with that.

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:37.590
I end up getting pregnant
again and we go through

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:39.800
a whole tour with me being pregnant

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:43.050
and for Michael, he feels
all this freedom in atheism

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.850
because he's not struggling anymore.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.270
For me, I'm feeling all this anxiety

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:50.870
because I want him to
believe a certain thing

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:53.120
and I want myself to
believe a certain thing.

00:04:53.341 --> 00:04:58.341
And I'm still just struggling
hard to belong and to be okay.

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:02.020
And I ended up having to quit a tour early

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:05.093
because I'm having, our baby's
having difficulty growing.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:09.460
She's born a month and a half early.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:12.880
She is just beautiful and
like with our first daughter,

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:14.840
we're both crying and
it's just this beautiful,

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:18.093
beautiful moment, and then she turns blue.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.580
I remember this nurse
coming over and she's

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:22.430
shaking and looking really worried.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:26.563
And she tells us our
daughter has Down Syndrome.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:29.840
And so in the days that
follow, we find out

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:34.110
that Lucy has two heart
issues and she has to have

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:35.960
a heart surgery her second day of life

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:37.440
and then she has to have
another heart surgery

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:38.740
when she's six months old.

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:41.263
Everything really changed for me.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.410
So I feel like this story
that I've been living

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:46.520
my whole life kind of came to this climax

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:48.263
with Lucy's birth.

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:52.383
When Lucy was born, we had
this huge social media blowup.

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:57.730
And there's stories in magazines
and all over the Internet

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:02.900
about our heresy, and we
were completely pushed out

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:06.380
of the church world, of this
tribe that we really loved,

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:09.323
and really painful and
devastating at so many of times.

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:12.560
Looking back on all of
it, I'm deeply grateful

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:14.310
for all of the things that happened

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:17.683
and I don't want what we used to have.

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:20.130
We live in a different head space now,

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:22.233
it's a completely different perspective.

00:06:22.749 --> 00:06:26.653
And the connection I
feel with my daughters,

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:30.640
there's no us verus them,
there's no you and I,

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:32.853
there's no winners and losers.

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:36.360
Part of my dream is that
people wouldn't be so afraid

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:37.373
and so scared.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:42.433
I know a lot of people are
still in this very conservative,

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:46.920
fundamental bubble and
they can be so afraid

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:48.560
to break out of that for fear

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:50.310
of what will happen to their lives.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:52.950
And this happens in any religion,

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:55.793
so my dream is that we're not so afraid.

00:06:56.684 --> 00:06:59.851
(contemplative music)

